DESCRIPTION:You <a><u></u></a>can create change for tenants in Prince Georg
 e by building collective power. Our first Tenants' Rights Workshop in Novem
 ber showed us that too many of our neighbors are struggling alone. We discu
 ssed issues like exploitative landlords and a lack of meaningful tenant adv
 ocacy. We believe that adequate housing is a human right. By coming togethe
 r\, you can help build a community of mutual support and find solutions to 
 housing injustice.<br><br><b>Who can attend?</b><br><br>Everyone is welcome
  to attend. To ensure our group is led by tenants for tenants\, only those 
 who do not own property can become a member or vote.<br><br><b>How can I he
 lp make this meeting successful?</b><br><br>Invite your family\, friends\, 
 and neighbors. You can share this post or print posters and handbills.<br><
 br>This event takes place on the traditional\, unceded territory of the Lhe
 idli T'enneh. We can not talk about housing justice without talking about t
 he displacement of Indigenous Peoples both past and present. No displacemen
 t on stolen land.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260214T004308Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Northern Tenants Union Meeting 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
